course: french
lesson: 8
title: Numbers 70 to 100: soixante-dix and quatre-vingts
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: In France the numbers from 70 to 99 are little sums: 70 is soixante-dix, sixty-ten, and 80 is quatre-vingts, four twenties.
explain: From 70 to 79 you keep saying soixante and add a number from 10 to 19: 71 is soixante et onze (60 + 11), 76 is soixante-seize (60 + 16).
explain: From 80 to 99 you say quatre-vingt and add a number from 1 to 19: 90 is quatre-vingt-dix (80 + 10), 99 is quatre-vingt-dix-neuf (80 + 19).
explain: English once counted in twenties too: Abraham Lincoln's "four score and seven years ago" means 87, because a score is 20.
explain: Picture bingo in Liverpool: the teacher calls "soixante-seize" and Ethan must wait for the whole number before he marks 76, not 60 or 16.
fact: soixante-dix ("swa-sahnt-DEESS") is 70, word for word sixty-ten.
fact: 71 is soixante et onze (60 + 11), 72 is soixante-douze, 73 is soixante-treize, and so on up to 79, soixante-dix-neuf.
fact: quatre-vingts ("katr-VAN") is 80, word for word four twenties.
fact: quatre-vingts has an s only when no other number follows it: 80 is quatre-vingts, but 81 is quatre-vingt-un, with no s and no et.
fact: 90 is quatre-vingt-dix (80 + 10); 91 is quatre-vingt-onze, 97 is quatre-vingt-dix-sept and 99 is quatre-vingt-dix-neuf.
fact: In Belgium and Switzerland 70 is septante and 90 is nonante; in Belgium 80 is still quatre-vingts, and in parts of Switzerland it is huitante. All are proper French.
fact: cent ("sahn") means a hundred; a euro cent is called un centime ("sahn-TEEM").
fact: Hyphens join all the parts of one number: quatre-vingt-huit is one number, 88, not four separate numbers.
fact: A score is 20 in old English, so "four score and seven" (Lincoln, 1863) is 87.
fact: Slang here: "bruv" means mate; "tamping" (Wales) means fuming; "my lover" (Bristol) means dear; "ma heid" (Scotland) means my head; "having a laugh" (UK) means joking; "la" (Liverpool) means mate; "I'm literally dead" means I can't cope (as a joke).
exercise: What is 70 in France? | soixante-dix | septante | sept-dix | soixante-et-dix
exercise: How do you say 71? | soixante et onze | soixante-dix-un | septante-un | soixante-onze-et
exercise: What is soixante-quinze? | 75 | 65 | 615 | 15
exercise: What does quatre-vingts mean word for word? | four twenties | four and twenty | forty | four hundred
exercise: How do you write 81? | quatre-vingt-un | quatre-vingts-un | quatre-vingt et un | quatre-vingts et un
exercise: When does quatre-vingts keep its s? | When no other number comes after it | Always, in every number from 80 to 99 | Only when you talk about money | Only after the word cent
exercise: What is 90 in France? | quatre-vingt-dix | nonante | neuf-dix | quatre-vingts-dix
exercise: What is 97? | quatre-vingt-dix-sept | quatre-vingt-sept | soixante-dix-sept | quatre-vingts-dix-sept
exercise: In Brussels a price is "septante euros". How much is it? | €70 | €17 | €700 | €7
exercise: In Belgium and Switzerland, what is 90? | nonante | neufante | quatre-vingt-neuf | nonze
exercise: What does cent mean on a French price tag? | a hundred | one euro cent | a pence | one-tenth
exercise: What is a euro cent called in everyday French? | un centime | un cent | un sou | un penny
exercise: Mia writes 99 in words. Which is right? | quatre-vingt-dix-neuf | quatre-vingts-dix-neuf | quatre-vingt-neuf | neuf-vingt-neuf
exercise: The teacher calls "soixante-seize". Which number is it? | 76 | 66 | 16 | 60
exercise: Ava's penpal's grandad is "quatre-vingt-huit ans". How old is he? | 88 | 4,208 | 84 | 98
exercise: The man says "quatre-vingt-quinze centimes". How much is that? | 95 cents | 4 euros 20 | 80 cents | 15 euros
test: Jayden says, "Sixty-ten?! Nah, bruv, that's maths homework." What's the best reply? | Yes, 70 is said as 60 + 10 in France | No, 70 is septante everywhere French is spoken | No, soixante-dix means sixteen | Yes, but only old people say it
test: Megan says 71 being "sixty and eleven" is "tamping". ("Tamping" means fuming.) What would 74 be? | soixante-quatorze | soixante-dix-quatre | septante-quatorze | soixante et quatorze
test: Ben's dad is impressed by "four score and seven". What number did Lincoln mean? | 87 | 47 | 74 | 107
test: Ivy's gran in Bristol asks, "Why's the s gone? That's proper weird, my lover." Ivy wrote "quatre-vingts-un". What's the rule? | The s stays only when no number follows | The s goes only on Fridays | The s goes because 81 is odd | The s moves to the end: quatre-vingt-uns
test: Ollie in Edinburgh groans, "Four twenty ten. Ma heid hurts." Which sum makes 90? | 4 × 20 + 10 | 4 + 20 + 10 | 40 + 20 + 10 + 20 | 4 × 10 + 20
test: A lady in Brussels says the price is "septante euros". Lily asks, "Isn't 70 soixante-dix? Was she having a laugh?" ("Having a laugh" means joking.) What is true? | Septante is proper French in Belgium and Switzerland | The Belgian lady made a mistake | Septante means 7 in Belgium | Septante is slang only teenagers use
test: Zac thinks "cent" means one cent. "Bargain, mate." What did it really cost? | 100 euros | 1 cent | 1 euro | 10 euros
test: Mia says, "That's like eleven syllables, I'm literally dead." How can she break up 99? | 80 + 19 | 9 + 9 | 90 + 9 said as nonante-neuf in France | 4 + 20 + 9 + 10 + 9
test: Ethan shouts, "Is that 60 or 16, la?" ("La" means mate.) The teacher said soixante-seize. What should he do? | Wait for the whole number and mark 76 | Mark 60 and 16 both | Mark 16, it came last | Mark 60, it came first
test: A cartoon penpal writes "Mon grand-père a quatre vingt huit ans" and Ava thinks he's 4,208. What would help her? | Add the parts: 4 × 20 + 8 = 88 | Read each word as a digit: 4, 20, 8 | Multiply everything: 4 × 20 × 8 | Ignore quatre and read 28
test: ★★★ Noah's mum pays a coin of "un euro" for something that costs "quatre-vingt-quinze centimes". How much change? | 5 cents | 15 cents | 25 cents | 95 cents
test: ★★★ Which of these is the biggest number? | quatre-vingt-dix-neuf | soixante-dix-neuf | quatre-vingt-neuf | quatre-vingt-huit
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the French numeral soixante-dix? | It denotes seventy and is formed as sixty plus ten | It denotes sixteen and is formed as six plus ten | It denotes six hundred and ten | It denotes seventy and is used solely in Belgium
exam: Identify the numeral denoted by the expression quatre-vingt-dix-neuf. | Ninety-nine | Eighty-nine | Four hundred and nineteen | Seventy-nine
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the terminal s of quatre-vingts. | It is retained solely where no further numeral follows | It is retained in every numeral from eighty to ninety-nine | It is omitted in every circumstance | It is retained solely in Switzerland
exam: It is given that in Belgium the numerals for seventy and ninety differ from those employed in France. State those numerals. | Septante and nonante | Soixante-dix and quatre-vingt-dix | Septante and huitante | Sept-dix and neuf-dix
